BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Celebrating Chrysanthemums
DTSTART:20261025T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:860ce5430bb7f1c3d095592192d5f3@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum’s annual John Lowell Gar
 dner Chrysanthemum Installation inspires Celebrating Chrysanthemums concer
 t on Sunday\, October 25\, an exploration of the flower as artistic muse h
 osted by the Gardner’s Stanley P. Kozak Director of Horticulture Erika R
 umbley and Abrams Curator of Music George Steel\, who will also read relat
 ed poems\, letters\, and horticultural texts. An all-star cast performs mu
 sic by Jules Massenet\, Léo Delibes\, Giacomo Puccini\, Scott Joplin\, Do
 ra Pejačević\, Nikolai Harito\, William Penn\, Zbigniew Maciejowski\, Er
 nesto Lecuona\, Tōru Takemitsu\, Xiaogang Ye\, and Juantio Becenti. The I
 sabella Stewart Gardner Museum’s Fall 2026 Weekend Concert Series featur
 es a ten-concert autumn season curated by Abrams Curator of Music George S
 teel held on select Sundays from September 13 through November 22\, 2026. 
 The fall season showcases world-class artists in the Museum’s extraordin
 ary Calderwood Hall—a 300-seat “sonic cube” with three levels of bal
 conies designed so that 80% of seats are front row\, creating a uniquely i
 ntense and intentional listening experience. Dating to 1927\, the Gardner
 ’s Weekend Concert Series is the longest running museum music program in
  the country. Learn More/Get Tickets Sources: Meet Boston Event page: http
 s://www.meetboston.com/event/celebrating-chrysanthemums/92815/\n\nEvents N
 ear Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallb
 ack from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.meetboston.com
 /event/celebrating-chrysanthemums/92815/
LOCATION:Isabella Stewart Gardner Museum\, 25 Evans Way\, Boston\, MA\, 02
 115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/celebrating-chrysanthemums/92815/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Choir concert: Tõnu Kõrvits\, composer
DTSTART:20261025T190000
DTEND:20261025T200000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:e228a8293c407aeaf497721f029db6@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:The Holy Cross College Choir will be performing a program of m
 usic from Scandinavia and the Baltics\, featuring Kreek’s Notebook by Aw
 ard-winning Estonian composer Tõnu Kõrvits. Estonia has a rich tradition
  of choral music. The country plays host to the Estonian Song Festival\, w
 hich started in 1869 and currently runs every five years\, is one of the l
 argest singing festivals in the world\, welcoming over 100\,000 people com
 ing together to unite in song. Kreek’s Notebook celebrates the rich heri
 tage of Estonian Choral Music through the use of native folk hymns collect
 ed by ethnomusicologist Cyrillus Kreek (1889–1962). Korvits weaves sacre
 d folk hymns and texts collected by Kreek into his own distinct musical la
 nguage. A multi-movement work for string orchestra and choir\, Kreek’s N
 otebook synthesizes traditional melodies with thrilling avant-garde string
  writing\, inviting the listener into moments of spiritual contemplation a
 nd visceral passion. Additional works on the program include music by Arvo
  Pärt\, Veljo Tormis\, Algirdas Martinaitis\, and Laura Jekabsone. Funded
  by The Patrick E. Moriarty\, M.D. '57 Visiting Scholars Program. Dress Co
 de: Casual (jeans ok) --- Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?i
 d=2152228 Source: College of the Holy Cross Event page: https://myhc.holyc
 ross.edu/rsvp?id=2152228\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northboroug
 h\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from worcester-colleges-events.ics
 \nSource page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152228
LOCATION:St. Joseph Memorial Chapel\, 1 College Street\, Worcester\, MA 01
 610\, United States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152228
END:VEVENT
