BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Reception and Artist Talk: “Paper and Stone: A Retrospective\,
 ” Tim de Christopher\, Open Door Gallery
DTSTART:20261025T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:25a30718ec3797d217c305d3842a7b@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Join us in the Open Door Gallery for the opening reception of 
 Paper and Stone: A Retrospective with artist Tim de Christopher. At 2 pm\,
  de Christopher will give an artist talk reflecting on his artistic proces
 s. Known for his stone carvings\, de Christopher’s works include a serie
 s of gargoyles created for the Jewish Museum in New York City and a public
  installation titled Rock Paper Scissors in Turners Falls\, MA. Paper and 
 Stone features works across mediums\, including stone carvings\, paintings
 \, prints\, and drawings. The exhibition showcases his legacy of creativit
 y\, humor\, and gift for elevating the everyday. Admission to the Open Doo
 r Gallery is always free. The Open Door Gallery at the Worcester Art Museu
 m is a gallery space for artists with disabilities\, created in partnershi
 p with Open Door Arts\, a program of Seven Hills Foundation. Sources: Disc
 over Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/e
 vent/reception-and-artist-talk%3a-%e2%80%9cpaper-and-stone%3a-a-retrospect
 ive-%e2%80%9d-tim-de-christopher-open-door-gallery/31102/\n\nEvents Near M
 e: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback f
 rom massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.o
 rg/event/reception-and-artist-talk%3a-%e2%80%9cpaper-and-stone%3a-a-retros
 pective-%e2%80%9d-tim-de-christopher-open-door-gallery/31102/
LOCATION:Worcester Art Museum\, 55 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/reception-and-artist-talk%3a-%
 e2%80%9cpaper-and-stone%3a-a-retrospective-%e2%80%9d-tim-de-christopher-op
 en-door-gallery/31102/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Richard\, Oscar and Lorenz on the Mighty Wurlitzer with Dr. Kleefi
 eld
DTSTART:20261025T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:db517b9645244ab1b25d8d0370a708@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Resident organist\, Dr. Jonathan Kleefield returns to the main
  stage with a new concert! Kicking off the upcoming season with a rousing 
 start\, Dr. Kleefield returns to the Mighty Wurlitzer to present the work 
 of 20th century musical and lyrical titans Richard Rodgers\, Oscar Hammers
 tein II and Lorenz Hart. These remarkable talents produced some of the era
 ’s most memorable songs\, including “Manhattan\,” “Blue Moon” an
 d “My Funny Valentine.” The program will also feature extended medleys
  from Rodgers and Hammerstein musicals\, including South Pacific\, The Kin
 g and I and The Sound of Music. As usual\, Dr. Kleefield will provide comm
 entary on the lives of these extraordinary creative talents and their musi
 cal creations. Don’t feel embarrassed if you want to hum or sing along! 
 The Mighty Wurlitzer\, assembled and gifted to the theatre by Donald Phipp
 s\, is recognized as one of the cultural jewels of Worcester. Phipps\, Kle
 efield and the Mighty Wurlitzer were recently highlighted on WGBH’s\, Th
 e Culture Show. As a board director of the Eastern Massachusetts Chapter o
 f the American Theatre Organ Society\, Phipps followed in the footsteps of
  our theatre’s founders\, with his vision of restoring a treasured piece
  of our heritage and culture. Learn more about how you can support this ma
 gnificent instrument. All-In Pricing: Tickets are $10 for non-members and 
 FREE for members\, subscribers\, current conservatory families and their g
 uests. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.dis
 covercentralma.org/event/richard-oscar-and-lorenz-on-the-mighty-wurlitzer-
 with-dr-kleefield/30973/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northboroug
 h\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSou
 rce page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/richard-oscar-and-lorenz
 -on-the-mighty-wurlitzer-with-dr-kleefield/30973/
LOCATION:The Hanover Theatre and Conservatory for the Performing Arts\, 2 
 Southbridge St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/richard-oscar-and-lorenz-on-th
 e-mighty-wurlitzer-with-dr-kleefield/30973/
END:VEVENT
