BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Talk: The Tortoise\, the Hare\, and the Art Market
DTSTART:20261025T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:623a1412da5a58dc07531021e7f103@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Museums work at a steady\, methodical pace. Exhibitions are pl
 anned months if not years in advance\, patrons are cultivated over years a
 nd decades to become donors\, and art is collected slowly in accordance wi
 th institutional vision. On the other hand\, auction houses move like ligh
 tning\, with ever-changing focuses. Entire auctions are put together and s
 old within two to three months. Client relationships\, though often long-l
 asting\, are usually built quickly and circumstantially and subject to the
  whims of the art market. Despite their difference in pace\, however\, mus
 eums and auction houses hold an important relationship\, supplementing and
  supporting art\, artists\, and each other. In this expert talk\, Robin St
 arr of Bonhams Boston (formerly Skinner) will share stories about her work
  with museums\, including a look behind the scenes at some of your favorit
 es in the Worcester Art Museum’s collection. Sources: Discover Central M
 assachusetts Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/talk%3a-t
 he-tortoise-the-hare-and-the-art-market/30998/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 3
 0 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massach
 usetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/ta
 lk%3a-the-tortoise-the-hare-and-the-art-market/30998/
LOCATION:Worcester Art Museum\, 55 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/talk%3a-the-tortoise-the-hare-
 and-the-art-market/30998/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:They Tried To Silence Us. We Became The Voice.
DTSTART:20261025T000000
DTEND:20261025T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:446985eeb643dda4ee32e329837f56@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:From this JMAC presenter: THEY TRIED TO SILENCE US. WE BECAME 
 THE VOICE. A Mini Independent Film Festival Celebrating Puerto Rican Stori
 es\, Resistance & Action Join us for an evening of independent Puerto Rica
 n filmmaking\, history\, culture\, and community dialogue. The program wil
 l feature three independent short films\, each offering a different story 
 and perspective\, leading into our featured headliner\, Mataron a Pedro 
 — a powerful film exploring the life\, legacy\, and historical significa
 nce of Dr. Pedro Albizu Campos. Following the screening\, we will gather f
 or a special Q&A and community panel featuring the film’s director and w
 riter/producer Debbie Perez of Borinken Podcast\, alongside three leaders 
 from grassroots collectives in the Puerto Rican diaspora. Together\, we wi
 ll explore the stories behind the films\, the history they preserve\, and 
 the responsibility that comes with knowing our history. But this conversat
 ion does not end with the credits. How do we turn education into action? H
 ow can the Puerto Rican diaspora support communities on the island? What d
 oes organizing look like today? And how do we move from learning about our
  history to becoming part of its future? This is more than a film screenin
 g. It is a space to remember\, learn\, connect\, organize\, and act. Becau
 se they tried to silence our voices. We became the voice. -- For more info
 rmation contact |Zorimar Rivera Fpunder/President raiceslibrema@gmail.com 
 Follow: IG & Facebook @raiceslibrema -- Trigger warnings: This program inc
 ludes mature themes and discussions of political repression\, violence\, i
 mprisonment\, colonialism\, and Puerto Rico's struggle for self-determinat
 ion. Viewer discretion is advised. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts
  Event page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/they-tried-to-silence
 -us-we-became-the-voice/30793/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of North
 borough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ic
 s\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/they-tried-to-sile
 nce-us-we-became-the-voice/30793/
LOCATION:Jean McDonough Arts Center\, 20 Franklin St.\, Worcester\, MA\, 0
 1608
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/they-tried-to-silence-us-we-be
 came-the-voice/30793/
END:VEVENT
