BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:A Tale of Murder in the Shadow of the American Revolution
DTSTART:20261029T000000
DTEND:20261029T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:cb81ebd118fe4933c9e3055ebd9132@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:In 1798\, a harrowing series of murders begins in Kentucky. Th
 e first body\, discovered by cattle drovers\, lies bloody at the bottom of
  a ridge. Then another—a dead boy staring up from a sinkhole. Bodies tur
 n up along roadsides\, stuffed into brush. They float to the surface of mu
 ddy brooks. For nine months\, over hundreds of miles of Kentucky and Tenne
 ssee countryside\, the terror unfolds. The killers—two men with hazy bac
 kgrounds—are brothers\, named Wiley and Micajah Harp. Drawing from her n
 ew book\, Kingdom of Devils: A Tale of Murder in the Shadow of the America
 n Revolution (2026)\, Katherine Grandjean investigates the historical mean
 ings of the Harps’ infamous spree\, revealing the dark side of the young
  United States’ independence. While the American Revolution was liberati
 ng to some\, it was also deeply destabilizing\, politically and socially\,
  to others. Grandjean unspools the mystery of what sent the Harps reeling 
 and exposes the hidden\, violent legacies of the revolutionary era. This p
 rogram will be held in person and livestreamed. Register for both options 
 here. Katherine Grandjean is associate professor of history at Wellesley C
 ollege. Her research explores early American history\, environmental histo
 ry\, and the roots of violence in American history. Her first book\, Ameri
 can Passage: The Communications Frontier in Early New England \, was publi
 shed in 2015. Grandjean was an AAS-National Endowment for the Humanities L
 ong-Term Fellow in 2017-18. She was elected to AAS membership in April 202
 1. Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.discove
 rcentralma.org/event/a-tale-of-murder-in-the-shadow-of-the-american-revolu
 tion/30657/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532
 \nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: ht
 tps://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-tale-of-murder-in-the-shadow-of-th
 e-american-revolution/30657/
LOCATION:American Antiquarian Society\, 185 Salisbury St.\, Worcester\, MA
 \, 01609
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/a-tale-of-murder-in-the-shadow
 -of-the-american-revolution/30657/
END:VEVENT
