BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Sovereign Science: Saving Our Red-Tailed and Raptor Relatives
DTSTART:20261029T183000
DTEND:20261029T193000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:2f1dc27e551ad5de0a4c39507481e6@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:For this special edition of Authors “Around” the Hill\, we
  are excited to welcome speakers from Sovereign Science\, an Indigenous ST
 EAM Think Tank that conducts community reflective research of our environm
 ent and the impacts of ecocide and climate change on all life. They will d
 iscuss their ongoing project mapping the mortality and migration of Red-Ta
 iled Hawks in New England and their approach to environmental and scientif
 ic research\, connecting nature and the environment with culture and under
 standing our diverse ecosystem. All are welcome to join in this illuminati
 ng conversation about Indigenous science\, sovereignty\, and how we can su
 pport the diverse species that live alongside us. Sovereign Science is an 
 ongoing initiative to better intersectional literacy in STEAM to positivel
 y impact indigenous ecosystems\, with Indigenous methodologies. As a think
 tank\, Sovereign Science has uplifted tribal and non-tribal citizen scienc
 e for ecological justice and sociopolitical advocacy. Since 2022\, Soverei
 gn Science has been researching the rodenticide concern alongside Indigeno
 us people’s observations in New England of redtail hawks in addition to 
 recurring fish populations and migratory paths. Sovereign Science work inc
 ludes participation at the United Nations in various high level political 
 forums around sustainable development\, migratory species and climate chan
 ge. Keshia Lawrence (she/they) is a Ramapough and Montaukett tribal member
 \, and a PhD student at Trent University. Casey Howell (he/him) is Mattake
 eset Massachusett and Saponi\, and a Sovereign Science team member. Learn 
 more about Sovereign Science and their work: Sovereign Science Collaborati
