SUMMARY:Autumn Adventures Weekend
DTSTART:20261031T000000
DTEND:20261101T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:adefa646b2fd5bbd341f05f33fbed1@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Date: October 31 — November 1\, 2026 10:00 am – 5:00 pm Ha
 ve you noticed changes in the leaves? A chill in the air? The start of a s
 pooky season? Autumn is here and we are getting into the Halloween spirit 
 at the EcoTarium. Explore ghostly bubbles\, go on an adventure in our Glow
  Zone or even celebrate Jack-O-Lanterns with some explosive experiments al
 l while learning about the science behind changing seasons! Costumes are e
 ncouraged (but not required) and join us for a happy\, haunted Halloween! 
 There is always something new happening both on our grounds and inside the
  museum building. For maximum fun\, experience one of our daily planetariu
 m programs*\, take a ride on the Worcester Railers Explorer Express Train*
  when operating seasonally\, and get up close to our resident otters*! *Re
 quires a separate ticket that is not included with admission. Get Tickets 
 to Visit! Sources: Discover Central Massachusetts Event page: https://www.
 discovercentralma.org/event/autumn-adventures-weekend/31016/\n\nEvents Nea
 r Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallbac
 k from massachusetts-events.ics\nSource page: https://www.discovercentralm
 a.org/event/autumn-adventures-weekend/31016/
LOCATION:EcoTarium\, 222 Harrington Way\, Worcester\, MA\, 01604
URL:https://www.discovercentralma.org/event/autumn-adventures-weekend/3101
 6/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Baby Bugs
DTSTART:20261031T000000
DTEND:20261031T000000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:4990fe12b555fe3969d60b325b49fb@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Baby Bugs is an alternative music project founded by Bowie. Ra
 ised on bluegrass guitar and church hymns\, Bowie spent years under the we
 ight of religious trauma and emotional abuse before discovering that writi
 ng songs and poems was the only way to clearly express themselves. In 2021
 \, at the age of 18\, Bowie released their first song\, “HeyBunny.” Th
 e track surpassed 2 million streams in its first 60 days and received an o
 utpouring of support from fans encouraging Baby Bugs to continue. Inspired
  by this response\, Bowie decided to keep writing and recording music with
  the goal of helping others who have experienced similar hardships feel le
 ss alone. Brooklyn-based artist Elliot Lee fuses dark pop melodies with ed
 gy vocals and innovative electronic rock soundscapes to create an unpredic
 table sound\, acting as a voice for the voiceless. Lee understands the pow
 er of music unhindered by norms and its impact on underrepresented communi
 ties. This bravado seeps through her homemade tracks\, which are laced wit
 h late-night slumber party confessions and existential awareness. Inspired
  by feelings of loneliness\, Lee’s music serves as a reminder that you a
 re never alone. Sources: Meet Boston Event page: https://www.meetboston.co
 m/event/baby-bugs/89993/\n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northboroug
 h\, MA 01532\nDiscovery: Local fallback from massachusetts-events.ics\nSou
 rce page: https://www.meetboston.com/event/baby-bugs/89993/
LOCATION:The Red Room at Cafe 939\, 939 Boylston St\, Boston\, MA\, 02115
URL:https://www.meetboston.com/event/baby-bugs/89993/
END:VEVENT
