BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Morton Feldman's Triadic Memories - Amy Williams\, piano
DTSTART:20261113T003000
DTEND:20261113T013000
DTSTAMP:20261025T151745Z
UID:9b77b0697b62470ea31a4609578986@events-near-me
DESCRIPTION:Morton Feldman’s extraordinary late solo piano work\, “Tri
 adic Memories” (1981) is a study in slowly evolving repetitions over the
  75-minute duration. The composer described the piece as “the biggest bu
 tterfly in captivity.” Exact repetitions\, subtle variations\, shifting 
 patterns and fresh new materials are interwoven. Materials are constantly 
 recontextualized\, using different voicing and registers\, changing one no
 te of a chord\, juxtaposing new harmonies—always changing and always sof
 t. The piece is not outwardly triadic (the harmonies are built entirely of
  seconds\, sevenths and augmented fourths)\, but triads emerge through the
  hazy resonance. Some materials happen only once\, while others are repeat
 ed\, varied and recontextualized. The listener is taken on a journey of de
 ep concentration and reflection. Pianist/composer Amy Williams has been co
 nnected to Feldman’s music since her childhood—her father and Feldman 
 were close colleagues at the University of Buffalo. She has recorded and p
 erformed his music for nearly three decades. Funded by The Patrick E. Mori
 arty\, M.D. '57 Visiting Scholars Program Dress Code: Casual (jeans ok) --
 - Event Details: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152230 Source: Colleg
 e of the Holy Cross Event page: https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152230
 \n\nEvents Near Me: within 30 miles of Northborough\, MA 01532\nDiscovery:
  Local fallback from worcester-colleges-events.ics\nSource page: https://m
 yhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152230
LOCATION:Brooks Concert Hall\, 1 College Street\, Worcester\, MA 01610\, U
 nited States
URL:https://myhc.holycross.edu/rsvp?id=2152230
END:VEVENT
